WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.170
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.440 --> 01:34.950
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.300 --> 01:37.890
[Episode 48]

4
01:38.640 --> 01:39.570
Comrade Zedong.

5
01:39.950 --> 01:42.120
Our vanguard has won a great victory.

6
01:42.509 --> 01:44.479
Surely we can’t just enjoy the fruits of their victory

7
01:44.479 --> 01:45.500
without sending them some token of thanks, can we?

8
01:45.500 --> 01:46.810
That's right.

9
01:48.390 --> 01:51.360
Ever since we set out on the Long March,

10
01:51.720 --> 01:53.550
I've been working on a poem.

11
01:53.750 --> 01:56.270
Today, I'd like to share it with you.

12
01:56.520 --> 01:57.490
Consider this a gesture of my respect.

13
01:57.490 --> 01:58.770
-All right! -Good.

14
02:02.800 --> 02:07.910
The Red Army fears not the trials of the March,

15
02:11.039 --> 02:15.430
holding light ten thousand crags and torrents.

16
02:17.200 --> 02:21.270
The Five Ridges wind like gentle ripples,

17
02:22.150 --> 02:25.800
and the majestic Wumeng roll by, globules of clay.

18
02:40.640 --> 02:45.170
Warm the steep cliffs lapped by the water of Jinsha.

19
02:51.290 --> 02:55.720
Cold the iron chains spanning the Tatu River.

20
02:58.850 --> 03:02.660
Minshan's thousand li of snow joyously crossed,

21
03:05.690 --> 03:10.380
the three Armies march on, each face glowing.

22
03:21.200 --> 03:23.590
On September 29, 1935,

23
03:24.370 --> 03:27.300
at Wenmiao Street Primary School in Tongwei County,

24
03:27.360 --> 03:30.990
Mao Zedong recited his poem "The Long March" for the first time.

25
03:31.360 --> 03:33.420
No one at the time could have imagined

26
03:33.800 --> 03:35.520
that these 56 characters

27
03:35.760 --> 03:37.460
would leave such a remarkable mark

28
03:37.460 --> 03:39.340
on the land of China.

29
03:39.850 --> 03:41.090
These 56 characters

30
03:41.390 --> 03:44.040
may make up the world's longest poem.

31
03:44.250 --> 03:46.560
It linked 12,500 kilometers of endless mountains and rivers

32
03:46.560 --> 03:48.180
through the trudging footsteps of the Red Army,

33
03:48.180 --> 03:50.090
forging a dual passage

34
03:50.150 --> 03:51.640
of history and spirit.

35
03:51.940 --> 03:53.260
These 56 characters

36
03:53.430 --> 03:55.040
record the miracle and glory of the Communist Party of China

37
03:55.040 --> 03:57.670
and the Red Army, who grew through suffering,

38
03:57.829 --> 03:58.780
broke out of dire straits,

39
03:58.780 --> 04:00.870
and carved out a path to survival

40
04:00.890 --> 04:02.610
and a brand-new future.

41
04:03.670 --> 04:05.200
These 56 characters

42
04:05.270 --> 04:06.520
fill us with awe as we look back.

43
04:06.520 --> 04:08.830
Let the mountains and rivers bear witness.

44
04:08.830 --> 04:10.990
Let the skies of history bear witness.

45
04:11.590 --> 04:14.920
When the sky was about to fall, they stood firm and held it up.

46
04:15.480 --> 04:18.230
The Chinese nation found its strongest backbone,

47
04:18.230 --> 04:19.820
its greatest courage,

48
04:20.230 --> 04:22.230
and its spine that would never bend.

49
04:24.080 --> 04:26.520
On October 2, 1935,

50
04:26.910 --> 04:28.880
the Shaanxi and Gansu Detachment of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army

51
04:28.880 --> 04:30.520
set out from Tongwei in three columns

52
04:30.520 --> 04:32.780
and continued north

53
04:32.890 --> 04:35.409
toward the Xi'an-Lanzhou Highway

54
04:35.520 --> 04:36.320
between Huining and Jingning.

55
04:36.320 --> 04:38.790
where the KMT troops had set up a blockade.

56
04:38.960 --> 04:40.270
Before the troops set out,

57
04:40.270 --> 04:42.200
Zhou Enlai, who no longer had the codebook

58
04:42.200 --> 04:44.320
for contacting the 2nd and 6th Army Corps,

59
04:44.320 --> 04:45.120
sent them

60
04:45.440 --> 04:48.080
a telegram in plain language.

61
04:47.490 --> 04:53.350
[Mogang'ai, Shimen County, Hunan]

62
04:48.150 --> 04:49.080
Comrades,

63
04:49.590 --> 04:51.440
first, I have some news to share.

64
04:52.760 --> 04:54.890
Our Counter-Encirclement Campaign,

65
04:54.960 --> 04:56.790
which lasted more than six months,

66
04:56.790 --> 04:59.350
has ended with the KMT troops in full retreat

67
04:59.300 --> 05:02.210
[Ren Bishi, Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee; Political Commissar of the 2nd Red Army Corps]

68
04:59.390 --> 05:02.270
and victory in our hands!

69
05:02.320 --> 05:04.390
-Great! -Excellent!

70
05:03.990 --> 05:05.510
[He Long, Corps Commander of the 2nd Red Army Corps]

71
05:05.590 --> 05:07.190
[Guan Xiangying, Deputy Political Commissar of the 2nd Red Army Corps]

72
05:10.150 --> 05:11.550
Over the past six months,

73
05:12.000 --> 05:14.600
we have used flexible tactics

74
05:14.790 --> 05:16.590
to fight an enemy 10 times our strength

75
05:16.590 --> 05:18.120
in more than 30 battles.

76
05:18.230 --> 05:20.030
We have killed or wounded over 10,000 enemy troops.

77
05:20.030 --> 05:21.680
That is a great victory!

78
05:23.350 --> 05:25.590
But we must also see it clearly that

79
05:25.880 --> 05:28.140
the current situation is not promising.

80
05:28.220 --> 05:30.030
Chiang Kai-shek is about to launch

81
05:30.030 --> 05:31.520
another encirclement campaign against us.

82
05:31.520 --> 05:32.590
And we...

83
05:34.320 --> 05:35.560
have no choice

84
05:35.870 --> 05:36.870
but to fight!

85
05:40.230 --> 05:41.200
Comrades,

86
05:41.470 --> 05:42.830
our top priority now

87
05:43.030 --> 05:46.470
is to improve the military skills of our officers and soldiers,

88
05:46.470 --> 05:49.130
and political education throughout the ranks.

89
05:49.200 --> 05:52.350
These are the two fists we use to strike the enemy.

90
05:52.640 --> 05:53.790
With solid military skills,

91
05:53.790 --> 05:55.390
we can defeat a powerful enemy

92
05:55.390 --> 05:57.200
on the battlefield.

93
05:57.390 --> 05:58.790
Only with firm political convictions

94
05:58.790 --> 06:01.170
can we keep our troops from going off track.

95
06:01.170 --> 06:04.970
The revolutionary situation is approaching a major turning point.

96
06:05.200 --> 06:08.320
The stronger our new Soviet base becomes,

97
06:08.320 --> 06:10.370
the better we can support the CPC Central Committee's

98
06:10.370 --> 06:13.120
strategy of marching north to resist Japanese aggression.

99
06:13.120 --> 06:14.790
Do you have confidence in our cause?

100
06:14.790 --> 06:17.390
-Yes! -Yes!

101
06:16.210 --> 06:17.710
[Meeting of Party Activists of the 2nd and 6th Army Groups of the Red Army]

102
06:17.390 --> 06:18.150
Good!

103
06:18.150 --> 06:21.270
Wonderful!

104
06:21.880 --> 06:23.880
Now, break into groups and discuss!

105
06:25.520 --> 06:26.570
Comrade Bishi,

106
06:26.960 --> 06:29.720
you really know how to deliver a speech. Well said.

107
06:29.720 --> 06:30.370
See?

108
06:30.400 --> 06:32.640
What you said truly resonated with all of us.

109
06:32.640 --> 06:33.640
Comrade He Long.

110
06:33.680 --> 06:35.600
These are everyone's true feelings.

111
06:35.600 --> 06:37.360
I was just putting them into words.

112
06:37.360 --> 06:38.690
You're still so modest.

113
06:39.170 --> 06:40.090
Come on. Let's go.

114
06:40.090 --> 06:41.300
Report!

115
06:44.920 --> 06:47.290
We just received a telegram in plain language.

116
06:47.290 --> 06:48.350
In plain language?

117
06:48.480 --> 06:49.790
Who sent it? What does it say?

118
06:49.790 --> 06:50.920
The signal was weak.

119
06:51.150 --> 06:52.909
Judging by the tone

120
06:53.000 --> 06:54.680
and the sending operator's technique,

121
06:54.680 --> 06:55.830
it seems to have come from the CPC Central Committee.

122
06:55.830 --> 06:57.360
The CPC Central Committee?

123
06:57.909 --> 07:00.120
Why would they send a telegram in plain language?

124
07:00.120 --> 07:00.950
Exactly.

125
07:05.590 --> 07:06.590
How about this?

126
07:07.560 --> 07:08.550
Let's use our code

127
07:08.550 --> 07:09.780
to send them a reply,

128
07:09.960 --> 07:11.120
so we can verify the sender's identity

129
07:11.120 --> 07:12.570
and make sure it's not a trap.

130
07:12.570 --> 07:13.900
Let's discuss it first.

131
07:15.320 --> 07:17.590
To verify that the telegram was genuine,

132
07:17.790 --> 07:20.120
Ren Bishi, He Long, and Guan Xiangying

133
07:20.120 --> 07:21.320
discussed the matter

134
07:21.390 --> 07:23.640
and sent the CPC Central Committee

135
07:23.710 --> 07:25.770
a coded telegram signed by Ren and He.

136
07:26.080 --> 07:28.970
In the telegram, they included a brief report on the 2nd and 6th Corps,

137
07:28.970 --> 07:32.240
and specifically asked, "Where are you now?

138
07:32.350 --> 07:33.780
We've been out of contact for a long time.

139
07:33.780 --> 07:35.150
In your reply,

140
07:35.350 --> 07:38.590
please name the members of our provincial committee

141
07:39.080 --> 07:41.150
to confirm your identity."

142
07:41.390 --> 07:43.030
As expected,

143
07:43.270 --> 07:44.400
this coded telegram

144
07:44.640 --> 07:47.000
was intercepted by Zhang Guotao,

145
07:45.890 --> 07:48.290
[Dangba, Sichuan]

146
07:47.000 --> 07:48.730
who had access to the codebook.

147
07:49.400 --> 07:53.110
[Zhang Guotao, Member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Politburo, Vice Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission, and Political Commissar-General of the Red Army]

148
07:50.230 --> 07:51.909
The 2nd and 6th Corps seem to have made

149
07:51.909 --> 07:55.170
good progress in the Hunan-Hubei-Sichuan-Guizhou area.

150
07:55.470 --> 07:57.200
They must be a sizable force by now, right?

151
07:57.200 --> 07:58.000
That's right.

152
08:00.680 --> 08:01.790
Send them a reply.

153
08:02.150 --> 08:03.120
Tell them

154
08:03.520 --> 08:05.050
the 1st and 4th Front Armies

155
08:05.120 --> 08:07.710
joined forces at Maogong County in mid-June.

156
08:07.930 --> 08:11.190
The CPC Central Committee appointed Comrade Zhang Guotao

157
08:11.760 --> 08:13.350
as General Political Commissar.

158
08:13.350 --> 08:14.960
And the provincial committee

159
08:14.960 --> 08:17.560
appointed Ren Bishi as secretary,

160
08:18.000 --> 08:18.730
with He Long,

161
08:18.830 --> 08:19.680
Xia Xi,

162
08:19.910 --> 08:20.910
Guan Xiangying,

163
08:21.080 --> 08:23.390
Xiao Ke, and Wang Zhen

164
08:23.520 --> 08:24.780
as committee members.

165
08:24.830 --> 08:26.290
Also tell them to maintain

166
08:26.710 --> 08:28.640
close contact with us from now on.

167
08:29.880 --> 08:31.480
How do we sign this telegram?

168
08:33.350 --> 08:34.950
Commander-in-Chief Zhu De,

169
08:36.080 --> 08:38.140
and General Political Commissar...

170
08:39.679 --> 08:40.480
Zhang Guotao.

171
08:40.690 --> 08:43.169
[Huang Chao, Secretary-General of the Northwest Revolutionary Military Commission and the Sichuan-Shaanxi Provincial Soviet Government]

172
08:42.620 --> 08:43.220
Yes, sir!

173
08:55.350 --> 08:56.590
We've now established

174
08:56.590 --> 08:59.710
our own revolutionary base areas

175
08:59.800 --> 09:01.830
in Yongshun, Sangzhi, and Longshan.

176
09:01.830 --> 09:04.140
But to consolidate our position here,

177
09:04.230 --> 09:06.800
we must first eliminate the local landlord militias.

178
09:06.800 --> 09:08.440
Issue this order to all officers at the company level and above.

179
09:08.440 --> 09:10.910
We need to continue political education among the people

180
09:10.910 --> 09:12.870
so they can wage class struggle themselves.

181
09:12.870 --> 09:13.330
Report!

182
09:13.490 --> 09:13.830
Go ahead.

183
09:13.830 --> 09:14.800
The supplies have arrived.

184
09:14.800 --> 09:15.800
Distribute them to all companies.

185
09:15.800 --> 09:16.350
Yes, sir!

186
09:16.510 --> 09:17.870
Corps Commander and Political Commissar.

187
09:17.870 --> 09:19.600
Headquarters has sent a reply.

188
09:20.710 --> 09:21.970
Let me see it. Quickly.

189
09:25.110 --> 09:26.110
Great.

190
09:26.360 --> 09:27.290
Brilliant!

191
09:27.310 --> 09:29.280
A reply from the Commander-in-Chief and the General Political Commissar

192
09:29.280 --> 09:31.440
carries the authority of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission.

193
09:31.440 --> 09:32.330
That's great!

194
09:32.360 --> 09:33.200
Comrades.

195
09:33.320 --> 09:35.320
We are no longer fighting alone.

196
09:35.440 --> 09:36.200
That's right.

197
09:36.200 --> 09:38.080
I suggest that we call a meeting of the Hunan-Hubei-Sichuan-Guizhou

198
09:38.080 --> 09:40.680
Provincial Committee and the Military Commission Subcommittee at once.

199
09:40.680 --> 09:42.600
Let's share this good news with the comrades,

200
09:42.600 --> 09:44.890
draw up our next operational plan

201
09:44.920 --> 09:45.650
and submit it to the Central Committee.

202
09:45.650 --> 09:46.130
Good.

203
09:46.260 --> 09:47.590
Bring the map, quickly.

204
09:48.510 --> 09:49.350
From then on,

205
09:49.850 --> 09:52.720
the 2nd and 6th Red Army Corps repeatedly asked the CPC Central Committee

206
09:52.720 --> 09:55.480
and the Central Red Army about the route they planned to take.

207
09:55.480 --> 09:58.040
Zhang Guotao sent telegrams signed "Zhu and Zhang,"

208
09:58.040 --> 10:00.350
but refused to reveal where the army was or what it planned.

209
10:00.350 --> 10:02.910
Unaware of the truth, Ren Bishi, He Long, and the others

210
10:02.910 --> 10:04.200
took the telegrams

211
10:04.440 --> 10:05.700
signed "Zhu and Zhang"

212
10:05.870 --> 10:08.280
to be genuine instructions from the Central Revolutionary Military Commission

213
10:08.280 --> 10:11.000
and kept communicating with Zhang Guotao.

214
10:11.840 --> 10:18.310
[Chengdu, Sichuan]

215
10:28.680 --> 10:30.210
Hanqing (Zhang Xueliang).

216
10:30.630 --> 10:31.590
Hanqing.

217
10:32.480 --> 10:33.050
Hanqing.

218
10:33.080 --> 10:34.010
Generalissimo.

219
10:35.840 --> 10:36.780
We're brothers, after all.

220
10:36.780 --> 10:38.180
There is no need for formalities.

221
10:38.030 --> 10:41.610
[Zhang Xueliang, Acting Commander-in-Chief of the Northwestern Bandit-Suppression Headquarters of the KMT Troops]

222
10:38.990 --> 10:39.920
Director Zhang.

223
10:40.140 --> 10:41.930
The Generalissimo heard you were coming,

224
10:41.930 --> 10:42.920
so he got up early today.

225
10:42.920 --> 10:43.890
He has asked

226
10:43.920 --> 10:44.690
seven times

227
10:44.720 --> 10:46.250
when your plane would land.

228
10:46.800 --> 10:49.400
I'm sorry to have worried you, Generalissimo.

229
10:51.230 --> 10:52.630
Yuanjing (He Guoguang),

230
10:52.710 --> 10:54.240
Chang Qing (Yang Yongtai).

231
10:54.300 --> 10:55.500
All right, all right.

232
10:55.510 --> 10:57.040
You two can get back to work.

233
10:57.040 --> 10:58.560
Let the two of us catch up.

234
10:58.680 --> 10:59.920
-Yes, Generalissimo. -Yes, Generalissimo.

235
10:59.920 --> 11:00.980
This way, Hanqing.

236
11:01.280 --> 11:02.810
After you, Generalissimo.

237
11:06.390 --> 11:07.150
Hanqing.

238
11:07.180 --> 11:07.870
Yes.

239
11:08.210 --> 11:09.770
As a man from the Northeast,

240
11:09.810 --> 11:11.930
are you getting used to the climate

241
11:11.960 --> 11:13.290
and food in Jiangcheng?

242
11:13.350 --> 11:14.160
Yes, I am.

243
11:14.710 --> 11:15.710
I'm a soldier.

244
11:15.800 --> 11:17.440
I do my best wherever I am.

245
11:18.160 --> 11:19.110
That's good.

246
11:20.040 --> 11:22.040
I've been thinking about you day and night.

247
11:22.040 --> 11:23.080
Now that I finally see you,

248
11:23.080 --> 11:25.800
half the weight on my mind is gone.

249
11:28.400 --> 11:30.590
I'm neither particularly capable nor well-educated,

250
11:30.590 --> 11:33.280
so I wonder how I could possibly ease your mind.

251
11:34.780 --> 11:36.440
A few days ago, I was on a plane,

252
11:36.470 --> 11:39.110
looking down at the mighty Yangtze River.

253
11:39.630 --> 11:41.230
I suddenly remembered something.

254
11:41.230 --> 11:42.830
On September 9th last year,

255
11:42.850 --> 11:44.410
didn't you organize

256
11:44.440 --> 11:46.830
a Yangtze River crossing competition?

257
11:47.160 --> 11:48.400
I remember it clearly, especially

258
11:48.400 --> 11:51.160
the trophy you presented to the winner.

259
11:51.280 --> 11:52.710
It was shaped like a silver shield,

260
11:52.710 --> 11:54.280
engraved with three words:

261
11:54.400 --> 11:55.870
"Turn the tide."

262
11:56.280 --> 11:57.540
What a powerful motto!

263
11:58.110 --> 11:59.080
You're too kind.

264
11:59.800 --> 12:01.470
You flatter me.

265
12:02.920 --> 12:04.800
I invited you to Chengdu this time

266
12:04.920 --> 12:07.750
because we have a tide to turn.

267
12:08.040 --> 12:08.920
As you know,

268
12:09.160 --> 12:10.490
the Zhu-Mao Communists

269
12:10.510 --> 12:11.960
have left southern Gansu

270
12:11.960 --> 12:13.470
and are heading straight to northern Shaanxi.

271
12:13.470 --> 12:14.920
If they join forces with Liu Zhidan

272
12:14.920 --> 12:16.590
and Xu Haidong,

273
12:16.920 --> 12:18.080
they will definitely become

274
12:18.080 --> 12:19.990
a major threat to the Party.

275
12:20.710 --> 12:22.680
So I plan to establish a

276
12:23.080 --> 12:25.160
Northwest Bandit Suppression Headquarters in Xi'an.

277
12:25.160 --> 12:26.040
I will be the Commander-in-Chief,

278
12:26.040 --> 12:26.990
and you will be the Deputy Commander-in-Chief,

279
12:26.990 --> 12:29.320
with authority to act on my behalf.

280
12:29.680 --> 12:30.560
Hanqing,

281
12:30.920 --> 12:33.110
you'll command not only the former Northeast Army

282
12:33.110 --> 12:33.870
but also

283
12:33.990 --> 12:36.300
troops from Shaanxi, Gansu, Ningxia, and Qinghai,

284
12:36.300 --> 12:38.060
plus some from Shanxi.

285
12:38.090 --> 12:40.400
That's 100,000 troops under your command!

286
12:40.400 --> 12:41.510
So, Hanqing,

287
12:42.110 --> 12:43.470
I'm thinking of entrusting you

288
12:43.470 --> 12:44.800
with the grand campaign

289
12:45.640 --> 12:47.240
to suppress the Communists.

290
12:52.870 --> 12:54.000
I've heard about it.

291
12:54.440 --> 12:56.710
This time, the Communist troops have marched north

292
12:56.710 --> 12:59.280
under the banner of resisting Japanese aggression.

293
12:59.280 --> 13:01.990
The Japanese want to impose

294
13:02.010 --> 13:03.490
"autonomy" on five provinces in North China,

295
13:03.490 --> 13:05.130
turning North China into

296
13:05.150 --> 13:07.280
another puppet state like Manchukuo.

297
13:08.560 --> 13:12.010
They're already making themselves at home there.

298
13:14.350 --> 13:15.630
Brother, when will you

299
13:16.190 --> 13:17.870
lead us to drive out

300
13:18.350 --> 13:19.610
the Japanese invaders

301
13:20.040 --> 13:21.560
and turn the tide?

302
13:22.440 --> 13:23.470
Hanqing,

303
13:24.080 --> 13:25.920
I know what's on your mind.

304
13:26.510 --> 13:28.110
Do you know why I've always insisted on

305
13:28.110 --> 13:30.160
"internal pacification before external resistance?"

306
13:30.160 --> 13:31.020
Let me explain.

307
13:31.320 --> 13:32.520
If you hadn't blocked

308
13:32.800 --> 13:34.590
traffic on the Yangtze River last year

309
13:34.590 --> 13:36.200
to keep foreign merchant ships

310
13:36.200 --> 13:38.710
from navigating freely,

311
13:39.110 --> 13:41.770
would you even have been able to hold that event?

312
13:49.280 --> 13:50.320
Generalissimo.

313
13:53.040 --> 13:53.990
Wait.

314
13:56.320 --> 13:57.400
Hanqing, sit down.

315
13:59.400 --> 14:00.080
Look,

316
14:00.230 --> 14:02.710
the pests we can see are above our heads,

317
14:02.750 --> 14:04.230
but the invisible parasites...

318
14:04.230 --> 14:06.560
are everywhere in the Party.

319
14:06.830 --> 14:08.890
And it's not just the Communist Army.

320
14:09.040 --> 14:09.870
Chen Jitang,

321
14:10.080 --> 14:12.040
Li Zongren, Bai Chongxi, Liu Xiang,

322
14:12.040 --> 14:14.440
He Jian, Wang Jialie and Long Yun,

323
14:14.560 --> 14:17.040
they are all parasites within the Party.

324
14:17.110 --> 14:18.350
Generalissimo.

325
14:19.560 --> 14:22.320
A great dike can collapse from a single ant hole,

326
14:22.680 --> 14:26.680
and a century-old beam can be hollowed out by termites.

327
14:28.630 --> 14:29.630
Let's go.

328
14:33.710 --> 14:34.990
I understand

329
14:35.410 --> 14:36.740
what you mean, Brother.

330
14:37.220 --> 14:38.820
There are parasites at home,

331
14:38.870 --> 14:40.590
and parasites abroad as well.

332
14:42.040 --> 14:43.840
Japan's cruel and greedy nature

333
14:43.920 --> 14:45.780
has now been completely exposed.

334
14:46.440 --> 14:49.080
This is a matter of our nation's very survival.

335
14:49.830 --> 14:51.890
I urge you to think it over carefully.

336
14:52.040 --> 14:52.830
Indeed.

337
14:52.870 --> 14:53.870
Hanqing.

338
14:54.320 --> 14:55.830
I know that, day and night,

339
14:55.830 --> 14:58.290
you long to avenge the loss of the Northeast.

340
14:58.870 --> 14:59.920
I, too, long to reclaim

341
14:59.920 --> 15:02.750
our territory with every breath I take.

342
15:03.110 --> 15:05.310
Once we've crushed the Communist army,

343
15:05.400 --> 15:07.630
I'll pour all of the nation's resources into retaking the Northeast.

344
15:07.630 --> 15:09.200
As brothers, you and I

345
15:09.680 --> 15:11.940
will fight our way back to the Northeast.

346
15:15.110 --> 15:18.370
If you are determined to fight our way back to the Northeast

347
15:18.870 --> 15:21.930
and rescue our 30 million people from this living hell,

348
15:22.440 --> 15:23.320
I, Xueliang,

349
15:25.080 --> 15:26.880
am willing to lead the vanguard.

350
15:28.920 --> 15:29.870
Hanqing,

351
15:35.560 --> 15:36.870
as brothers, you and I

352
15:37.750 --> 15:39.040
must work together

353
15:40.040 --> 15:41.440
to turn the tide.

354
15:43.800 --> 15:44.870
Yes!

355
15:50.280 --> 15:52.470
On October 2, 1935,

356
15:52.870 --> 15:55.590
just as the Kuomintang Government announced Zhang Xueliang's appointment

357
15:55.590 --> 15:58.990
as Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Northwest Bandit Suppression Headquarters,

358
15:58.990 --> 16:02.040
he received a report of a major defeat at Laoshan.

359
16:02.550 --> 16:04.910
The newly formed 15th Red Army Corps,

360
16:04.940 --> 16:07.320
under the command of Xu Haidong and other leaders,

361
16:07.320 --> 16:09.180
engaged in five hours of fierce fighting

362
16:09.180 --> 16:10.300
in the Laoshan area,

363
16:10.300 --> 16:12.370
annihilating most of the 110th Division

364
16:12.370 --> 16:14.160
of Wang Yizhe's Northeast Army.

365
16:14.160 --> 16:16.440
The operation killed or wounded over 1,000 troops,

366
16:16.440 --> 16:17.690
including Division Commander He Lizhong,

367
16:17.690 --> 16:19.970
and captured more than 3,700 prisoners.

368
16:20.350 --> 16:22.040
Since its founding, the 15th Red Army Corps

369
16:22.040 --> 16:23.270
had won its first battle,

370
16:23.270 --> 16:26.470
dealing a heavy blow to the enemy forces in the Northwest.

371
16:30.110 --> 16:31.200
According to the preliminary tally,

372
16:31.200 --> 16:32.180
we captured

373
16:31.410 --> 16:35.540
[Laoshan, Ganquan County, Shaanxi]

374
16:32.230 --> 16:33.460
more than 300 warhorses,

375
16:33.460 --> 16:34.500
4 mountain guns,

376
16:34.520 --> 16:35.470
8 mortars,

377
16:35.620 --> 16:37.590
over 180 light and heavy machine guns,

378
16:37.590 --> 16:39.790
and more than 3,000 rifles and pistols.

379
16:39.800 --> 16:40.560
Would you

380
16:40.710 --> 16:42.080
call this

381
16:42.080 --> 16:43.340
a welcome gift from the

382
16:43.590 --> 16:45.010
Northwest Bandit Suppression Headquarters?

383
16:45.010 --> 16:45.870
Of course it is!

384
16:45.880 --> 16:46.790
It's a big gift.

385
16:48.490 --> 16:49.400
This proves that

386
16:49.400 --> 16:50.320
Comrade Haidong's earlier strategy

387
16:50.320 --> 16:51.830
of striking the snake's head first

388
16:51.830 --> 16:52.830
was the right one.

389
16:53.830 --> 16:55.830
Everyone deserves credit for this.

390
16:55.830 --> 16:56.730
Fighting a war is like

391
16:56.730 --> 16:58.350
firing a kiln when I was a child.

392
16:58.350 --> 16:59.560
Someone has to mix the clay,

393
16:59.560 --> 17:01.680
someone has to shape the unfired pieces, and someone has to tend the fire,

394
17:01.680 --> 17:03.560
only then can you turn out good pottery.

395
17:03.560 --> 17:05.180
Take the ambush point at Laoshan, for example.

396
17:05.180 --> 17:06.900
Didn't you pick it, Liu?

397
17:07.710 --> 17:10.069
We're all revolutionary kiln workers,

398
17:10.160 --> 17:11.550
tending the fire together in northern Shaanxi

399
17:11.550 --> 17:12.329
and making it blaze even brighter.

400
17:12.329 --> 17:13.000
Well said!

401
17:13.560 --> 17:14.430
Report.

402
17:19.230 --> 17:20.230
Leaders,

403
17:20.030 --> 17:23.780
[Liu Huaqing, Section Chief of the Publicity Section, Political Department of the 15th Red Army Corps]

404
17:20.480 --> 17:22.339
while clearing the battlefield,

405
17:22.440 --> 17:24.119
our soldiers found a newspaper.

406
17:24.119 --> 17:26.150
It has news about the Central Red Army.

407
17:26.150 --> 17:26.710
What?

408
17:31.020 --> 17:31.760
What does it say?

409
17:31.760 --> 17:34.380
[Cheng Zihua, Political Commissar of the 15th Red Army]

410
17:31.910 --> 17:33.880
The Central Red Army has entered Gansu,

411
17:33.880 --> 17:34.510
heading north

412
17:34.450 --> 17:36.580
[Xu Haidong, Corps Commander of the 15th Red Army]

413
17:34.640 --> 17:36.370
towards the Guanzhong region.

414
17:36.750 --> 17:37.510
Great.

415
17:38.160 --> 17:40.440
Guanzhong is not far from here.

416
17:40.300 --> 17:44.350
[Liu Zhidan, Deputy Commander and Chief of Staff of the 15th Red Army]

417
17:40.470 --> 17:41.360
I suggest

418
17:41.600 --> 17:44.270
our 15th Red Army move west from Qingyang

419
17:44.430 --> 17:45.550
to meet up with the Central Red Army.

420
17:45.550 --> 17:46.270
All right.

421
17:47.330 --> 17:49.250
Zihua, what do you think?

422
17:49.690 --> 17:50.890
We're still surrounded

423
17:50.890 --> 17:52.880
by over a dozen Kuomintang divisions.

424
17:52.880 --> 17:55.100
I'm worried that moving west from Qingyang now

425
17:55.100 --> 17:57.100
will draw the enemy that way, too.

426
18:00.020 --> 18:01.210
How about this?

427
18:02.160 --> 18:03.200
We don't go west.

428
18:03.230 --> 18:04.470
We keep fighting south

429
18:04.470 --> 18:06.320
to draw the enemy forces around Xi'an toward us,

430
18:06.320 --> 18:08.920
giving the Central Red Army room to move north.

431
18:09.360 --> 18:10.160
Good.

432
18:10.440 --> 18:11.880
We'll do whatever helps

433
18:11.960 --> 18:12.990
the Central Red Army's march north.

434
18:12.990 --> 18:13.750
Right.

435
18:14.320 --> 18:17.140
Then let's try to take out a few more enemy strongholds.

436
18:17.140 --> 18:19.550
We've already received Chiang's welcome gift.

437
18:19.550 --> 18:20.400
So we'd better prepare a generous gift

438
18:20.400 --> 18:22.680
for the CPC Central Committee

439
18:22.710 --> 18:24.110
and the Central Red Army.

440
18:25.360 --> 18:25.890
Let's go.

441
18:25.920 --> 18:26.920
Come on, let's work out the plan.

442
18:26.920 --> 18:27.720
Come on.

443
18:29.770 --> 18:34.580
[Baisha Lama Temple, Zhuomudiao, Sichuan]

444
18:30.200 --> 18:31.120
Comrades,

445
18:32.660 --> 18:34.590
the Red Army must have discipline.

446
18:35.470 --> 18:37.270
But what exactly is discipline?

447
18:38.230 --> 18:39.830
Discipline is the guarantee

448
18:39.880 --> 18:42.470
that we carry out the correct line.

449
18:43.400 --> 18:44.360
Discipline is the guarantee

450
18:44.360 --> 18:45.520
that we reject

451
18:46.350 --> 18:48.740
the policy of fleeing north!

452
18:53.310 --> 18:54.310
Tell me,

453
18:54.710 --> 18:56.990
can a Central Committee that "flees" north

454
18:56.990 --> 18:58.750
still have any authority to lead?

455
18:58.750 --> 18:59.990
How is such a Central Committee

456
18:59.990 --> 19:02.270
qualified to lead the Red Army?

457
19:03.640 --> 19:04.970
I think we should follow

458
19:05.070 --> 19:08.230
Comrade Lenin's example

459
19:08.600 --> 19:11.310
in breaking with the Second International,

460
19:11.750 --> 19:13.440
and set up a new,

461
19:17.640 --> 19:21.140
provisional Central Committee.

462
19:41.400 --> 19:42.860
Commander-in-Chief Zhu,

463
19:44.310 --> 19:45.310
what do you think?

464
19:46.030 --> 19:47.290
Comrade Zhang Guotao,

465
19:47.820 --> 19:49.300
if I heard correctly,

466
19:49.920 --> 19:52.450
you want to set up another Central Committee.

467
19:53.680 --> 19:55.210
We can discuss it together.

468
19:55.390 --> 19:56.670
Your speech just now

469
19:56.900 --> 19:58.750
didn't sound like a discussion.

470
19:59.150 --> 20:00.350
And how can something like this

471
20:00.350 --> 20:03.400
be "discussed" so casually?

472
20:13.990 --> 20:14.840
Comrades!

473
20:15.360 --> 20:16.270
Comrades!

474
20:16.750 --> 20:17.990
I'll say it again:

475
20:18.640 --> 20:21.900
we are all Red Army soldiers under the Party's leadership.

476
20:22.270 --> 20:24.330
With the powerful enemy at our gates,

477
20:24.360 --> 20:25.690
we must stand together.

478
20:26.030 --> 20:28.120
If we split from within,

479
20:28.200 --> 20:30.510
we'll only weaken the Red Army

480
20:30.710 --> 20:33.640
and give the enemy a chance to destroy us.

481
20:33.660 --> 20:35.710
Comrades, the losses would far exceed the gains!

482
20:35.710 --> 20:37.400
So you still support that Central Committee?

483
20:37.400 --> 20:38.270
Which one?

484
20:38.400 --> 20:39.960
There is no such thing as "this" one and "that" one.

485
20:39.960 --> 20:41.710
There is only one CPC Central Committee,

486
20:41.710 --> 20:43.620
and it is the one

487
20:44.270 --> 20:45.800
leading the Red Army north!

488
20:55.070 --> 20:55.880
Comrades,

489
20:56.230 --> 20:57.440
please believe me.

490
20:57.880 --> 20:59.360
No matter how serious our disagreements are,

491
20:59.360 --> 21:02.020
they remain an internal matter for the Red Army.

492
21:06.750 --> 21:08.840
We must never split from the CPC Central Committee.

493
21:08.840 --> 21:09.960
That would be

494
21:10.070 --> 21:11.840
a grave betrayal of the Party.

495
21:13.600 --> 21:14.990
The Commander-in-Chief is right.

496
21:14.990 --> 21:17.200
Currently, we haven't yet

497
21:17.310 --> 21:18.960
turned the military situation around.

498
21:18.960 --> 21:21.710
A split would have serious consequences.

499
21:22.760 --> 21:25.130
[Dong Zhentang, Commander of the 5th Red Army]

500
21:22.880 --> 21:24.440
The Red Army must stay united!

501
21:24.440 --> 21:25.310
We cannot split!

502
21:25.310 --> 21:26.600
Yes, the Red Army must stay united!

503
21:26.600 --> 21:27.530
We cannot split!

504
21:27.550 --> 21:29.210
Marching north is flightism.

505
21:29.410 --> 21:31.160
Since when has marching north been "flightism"?

506
21:31.160 --> 21:32.700
Our march to the north is to resist Japanese aggression!

507
21:32.700 --> 21:34.760
Going north is to fight the Japanese!

508
21:34.960 --> 21:36.270
Chairman Zhang is right!

509
21:36.270 --> 21:37.550
What are you shouting about?

510
21:37.550 --> 21:39.150
What are you shouting about?

511
21:39.800 --> 21:41.430
Let Comrade Guotao finish.

512
22:02.640 --> 22:03.760
I now announce

513
22:05.400 --> 22:07.030
the new Central Committee

514
22:07.470 --> 22:09.600
and the list of its Politburo members.

515
22:09.610 --> 22:12.400
While the Red 15th Red Army Corps in northern Shaanxi

516
22:12.400 --> 22:15.960
was greeting the Central Red Army with a victory,

517
22:16.230 --> 22:18.060
a highly tense meeting

518
22:18.470 --> 22:20.600
of senior cadres was under way

519
22:20.750 --> 22:23.270
far away in Zhuomudiao, Lifan.

520
22:24.120 --> 22:26.400
At the Zhuomudiao meeting, Zhang Guotao

521
22:26.450 --> 22:28.790
brazenly announced the establishment of a so-called

522
22:28.790 --> 22:29.940
"CPC Central Committee,"

523
22:29.940 --> 22:31.040
"Central Government,"

524
22:31.040 --> 22:33.400
"Central Revolutionary Military Commission,"

525
22:33.400 --> 22:34.700
and "Central Committee of the Communist Youth League."

526
22:34.700 --> 22:37.440
He announced the dismissal of Mao Zedong, Zhou Enlai,

527
22:37.440 --> 22:39.610
Zhang Wentian, and Bo Gu,

528
22:39.640 --> 22:40.780
"expelled them from the Party,"

529
22:40.780 --> 22:42.380
and ordered their "arrest."

530
22:42.860 --> 22:44.890
Ye Jianying, Yang Shangkun, and others

531
22:44.890 --> 22:46.260
were "removed from office and placed under investigation."

532
22:46.260 --> 22:47.060
By this point,

533
22:47.440 --> 22:50.750
his differences with the CPC Central Committee over strategic line

534
22:50.750 --> 22:51.790
had escalated into

535
22:51.790 --> 22:54.850
an open political and organizational confrontation.

536
22:58.360 --> 23:01.160
Zhang Guotao, if you insist on having your own way,

537
23:01.160 --> 23:02.030
from today on,

538
23:02.440 --> 23:03.700
I, Zhu De, will continue

539
23:03.700 --> 23:06.220
my revolutionary work in my own name.

540
23:06.400 --> 23:11.130
I'll never oppose the Central Committee's decision to march north and resist Japan.

541
23:21.440 --> 23:23.040
Commander-in-Chief Zhu De,

542
23:23.070 --> 23:25.840
you have every right to hold on to your own views.

543
23:26.120 --> 23:28.780
But you are still the Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission

544
23:28.780 --> 23:31.030
and the Commander-in-Chief of the Red Army.

545
23:31.030 --> 23:32.140
I also believe

546
23:32.840 --> 23:35.500
that sooner or later, you'll return to our side.

547
23:37.960 --> 23:39.440
As for which one is right,

548
23:40.710 --> 23:41.500
history...

549
23:43.310 --> 23:44.470
will be the judge.

550
23:44.730 --> 23:45.640
You are right.

551
23:46.070 --> 23:47.470
I also believe

552
23:48.680 --> 23:50.410
that history will be the judge.

553
23:56.960 --> 23:58.160
Pass this file around

554
23:58.510 --> 23:59.920
and read it.

555
24:00.640 --> 24:02.040
Study it for yourselves.

556
24:39.210 --> 24:40.740
What's got you so worked up?

557
25:12.280 --> 25:14.230
Zhang Guotao came to me after the meeting.

558
25:14.230 --> 25:14.990
He said that

559
25:15.400 --> 25:18.550
if I recognized his newly established "Central Committee,"

560
25:18.550 --> 25:21.150
he'd give me a seat on the Military Commission.

561
25:21.640 --> 25:23.500
Otherwise, I wouldn't get a seat.

562
25:23.510 --> 25:24.710
What did you tell him?

563
25:25.990 --> 25:26.880
I won't

564
25:27.070 --> 25:28.440
fall for his tricks.

565
25:29.070 --> 25:30.030
I told him

566
25:30.510 --> 25:32.510
I didn't agree with what he was doing.

567
25:32.510 --> 25:33.710
And I had no interest

568
25:33.960 --> 25:35.790
in serving on that Military Commission.

569
25:35.790 --> 25:37.160
I've already handed over my duties

570
25:37.160 --> 25:39.620
and gone to teach at the Red Army University.

571
25:41.200 --> 25:44.400
Bocheng, we've been through so much together.

572
25:45.120 --> 25:46.200
We know each other inside out.

573
25:46.200 --> 25:48.060
I have no doubt about your loyalty

574
25:48.230 --> 25:49.960
to the Party and to the Red Army.

575
25:50.790 --> 25:52.160
This is the third time

576
25:52.230 --> 25:54.990
you've been removed as Chief of the General Staff, right?

577
25:54.990 --> 25:57.190
In 1927, during the Nanchang Uprising,

578
25:57.230 --> 25:58.920
you were the Chief of the General Staff.

579
25:58.920 --> 26:01.270
In 1932, when you arrived at the Central Soviet Area,

580
26:01.270 --> 26:02.960
you were the Chief of the General Staff.

581
26:02.960 --> 26:05.420
After the Xiang River Battle last December,

582
26:05.510 --> 26:07.550
they made you Chief of the General Staff once again.

583
26:07.550 --> 26:08.710
And look at me now.

584
26:08.840 --> 26:11.120
The first time I stepped down was because of a defeat.

585
26:11.120 --> 26:11.960
The last two times,

586
26:11.960 --> 26:14.490
it was simply because someone didn't like me.

587
26:14.750 --> 26:17.280
Three times as the Chief of the General Staff:

588
26:17.360 --> 26:19.490
one ended by defeat, two by dismissal.

589
26:21.990 --> 26:23.250
Commander-in-Chief,

590
26:23.310 --> 26:25.160
let's put my personal affairs aside.

591
26:25.160 --> 26:26.470
Zhang Guotao

592
26:26.920 --> 26:28.310
certainly knows how to play his cards.

593
26:28.310 --> 26:30.310
You see, he kept emphasizing

594
26:30.470 --> 26:32.110
discipline at today's meeting.

595
26:32.110 --> 26:33.880
He said discipline

596
26:34.230 --> 26:37.230
is the guarantee of carrying out the correct line.

597
26:37.470 --> 26:38.360
Discipline is what guards

598
26:38.360 --> 26:41.070
against the "flight line" to the north.

599
26:41.400 --> 26:42.750
How ironic,

600
26:42.880 --> 26:44.160
coming from him.

601
26:44.440 --> 26:45.960
Those are precisely the principles of discipline

602
26:45.960 --> 26:48.230
that the CPC Central Committee has always emphasized to him.

603
26:48.230 --> 26:51.400
But many of our comrades in the 4th Front Army

604
26:51.510 --> 26:53.370
have been deceived by his tricks.

605
26:53.680 --> 26:55.070
Zhang Guotao

606
26:55.840 --> 26:57.370
knows how to play politics.

607
26:57.920 --> 26:59.040
If he hadn't said those things,

608
26:59.040 --> 27:00.550
how could the officers and soldiers of the 4th Front Army

609
27:00.550 --> 27:01.880
be persuaded to follow him?

610
27:01.880 --> 27:03.790
He is twisting the facts

611
27:04.160 --> 27:05.680
and using deception and threats

612
27:05.680 --> 27:07.940
to drag the 4th Front Army along with him.

613
27:10.160 --> 27:10.960
However,

614
27:11.230 --> 27:14.230
not everyone has been taken in.

615
27:14.440 --> 27:16.600
I've seen that many comrades

616
27:16.680 --> 27:18.310
from the former 1st Front Army

617
27:18.310 --> 27:20.400
disapprove of his setting up another "Central Committee."

618
27:20.400 --> 27:21.460
That is a good sign.

619
27:21.880 --> 27:22.710
Besides,

620
27:23.400 --> 27:24.580
at today's meeting,

621
27:25.310 --> 27:26.250
I also noticed that

622
27:26.250 --> 27:28.490
many cadres of the 4th Front Army

623
27:28.750 --> 27:30.410
didn't agree with him either.

624
27:31.360 --> 27:32.390
Take Comrade Xiangqian,

625
27:32.390 --> 27:33.640
for example.

626
27:33.990 --> 27:36.200
He didn't speak up or state his position.

627
27:36.200 --> 27:37.230
Clearly,

628
27:37.600 --> 27:40.470
he didn't agree with Zhang Guotao's actions either.

629
27:40.470 --> 27:41.530
I noticed that too.

630
27:41.640 --> 27:43.120
In the 4th Front Army,

631
27:43.440 --> 27:46.370
Comrade Xiangqian's stance carries a lot of weight.

632
27:47.470 --> 27:49.470
So we mustn't lose heart.

633
27:49.600 --> 27:52.780
We should keep working to bring more comrades over to our side.

634
27:52.780 --> 27:55.410
Things will become clear sooner or later.

635
27:55.710 --> 27:58.270
Zhang Guotao can't overturn everything by himself.

636
27:58.270 --> 27:59.900
His so-called "CPC Central Committee"

637
27:59.900 --> 28:01.930
is a hollow imitation

638
28:02.030 --> 28:03.030
with no real authority.

639
28:03.030 --> 28:04.430
Commander-in-Chief...

640
28:04.470 --> 28:05.990
what worries me is that Zhang Guotao

641
28:05.990 --> 28:07.360
may plot behind our backs

642
28:07.360 --> 28:10.220
and retaliate against those who disagree with him.

643
28:10.790 --> 28:11.880
He’s done that

644
28:12.070 --> 28:13.530
many times over the years.

645
28:14.510 --> 28:15.430
You're right.

646
28:16.310 --> 28:17.970
We mustn't let our guard down.

647
28:18.070 --> 28:20.360
We need to be prepared for any

648
28:20.710 --> 28:23.490
extreme measures Zhang Guotao might take.

649
28:24.920 --> 28:25.680
Okay.

650
28:45.840 --> 28:47.440
I made my position

651
28:48.640 --> 28:51.270
very clear at the meeting.

652
28:52.840 --> 28:56.080
I hope we can stay united in our approach.

653
28:56.130 --> 28:59.060
[Xu Xiangqian, Commander-in-Chief of the 4th Front Army]

654
28:56.990 --> 28:58.120
Today, in this room,

655
28:58.120 --> 28:59.440
it's just the three of us.

656
28:59.170 --> 29:01.500
[Chen Changhao, Director of the Red Army's General Political Department; Political Commissar of the 4th Front Army]

657
28:59.990 --> 29:01.840
I want to hear your thoughts,

658
29:02.470 --> 29:03.600
your real thoughts.

659
29:06.880 --> 29:08.070
I didn't expect you

660
29:09.310 --> 29:10.750
to make such a bold move

661
29:12.030 --> 29:13.750
at that meeting.

662
29:18.790 --> 29:19.840
Changhao,

663
29:20.600 --> 29:21.640
go ahead.

664
29:26.200 --> 29:27.790
By the rules,

665
29:28.230 --> 29:29.750
Central Committee members

666
29:29.750 --> 29:31.200
must be elected

667
29:31.220 --> 29:32.960
at the National Party Congress.

668
29:32.960 --> 29:34.290
The central leadership

669
29:35.010 --> 29:37.810
must be approved by the Communist International.

670
29:37.880 --> 29:39.680
These are extraordinary times.

671
29:42.270 --> 29:44.880
Desperate times call for desperate measures.

672
29:44.990 --> 29:47.100
But do desperate measures

673
29:50.230 --> 29:51.960
definitely solve the problem?

674
29:54.230 --> 29:56.160
If we don't handle this carefully,

675
29:56.160 --> 29:58.160
the whole movement could collapse.

676
29:59.790 --> 30:00.920
So,

677
30:01.750 --> 30:03.410
neither of you agrees with me?

678
30:03.840 --> 30:04.960
Comrade Changhao

679
30:05.070 --> 30:06.840
has already made his position clear.

680
30:06.840 --> 30:09.070
First, this violates Party procedure.

681
30:09.280 --> 30:10.310
Second...

682
30:14.790 --> 30:16.070
Comrade Lenin

683
30:16.750 --> 30:18.900
founded the Third International

684
30:19.230 --> 30:20.750
to fight revisionism,

685
30:21.230 --> 30:23.030
opening a bright path

686
30:23.270 --> 30:25.730
for the international communist movement.

687
30:27.070 --> 30:28.790
Why can't we do the same?

688
30:28.930 --> 30:31.000
Can you really compare the two?

689
30:32.230 --> 30:34.160
Ours is an internal Party dispute.

690
30:34.200 --> 30:36.810
We can resolve all these problems

691
30:37.200 --> 30:38.090
through patient discussion,

692
30:38.090 --> 30:40.440
because they're disagreements within the Party.

693
30:40.440 --> 30:41.790
But what have you done now?

694
30:41.790 --> 30:42.600
"Expulsion."

695
30:42.840 --> 30:43.420
"Arrest warrants."

696
30:43.420 --> 30:44.840
"Two CPC Central Committees."

697
30:44.840 --> 30:48.450
Doesn't that delight our enemies and break the hearts of our own comrades?

698
30:48.450 --> 30:50.980
Haven't I tried to talk it through patiently?

699
30:51.030 --> 30:53.440
I told them time and again

700
30:53.680 --> 30:54.610
that going north

701
30:55.510 --> 30:57.760
is not a way out, but a dead end.

702
30:58.120 --> 31:01.360
I addressed the problems with going north one by one.

703
31:01.550 --> 31:04.840
I laid out the advantages of going south one by one.

704
31:04.960 --> 31:05.890
Did they listen?

705
31:07.360 --> 31:09.020
They simply wouldn't listen.

706
31:09.240 --> 31:10.530
They just couldn't see

707
31:10.710 --> 31:13.170
that moving south is the inevitable course!

708
31:13.200 --> 31:14.290
And now this "inevitable course" of yours

709
31:14.290 --> 31:15.940
has split the Red Army.

710
31:15.990 --> 31:17.750
Isn't leaving without a word a split?

711
31:17.750 --> 31:19.750
They left overnight without a word.

712
31:20.310 --> 31:21.360
Isn't that a split?

713
31:21.360 --> 31:22.330
That was the Central Committee's decision.

714
31:22.330 --> 31:23.160
They are two different things.

715
31:23.160 --> 31:24.490
They are the same thing.

716
31:24.550 --> 31:25.510
Think about it.

717
31:25.680 --> 31:27.640
When they set off from Ruijin,

718
31:27.990 --> 31:29.650
they had more than 80,000 men.

719
31:30.230 --> 31:31.690
And after joining forces?

720
31:31.960 --> 31:35.020
There were barely 10,000 men left, in rags.

721
31:35.840 --> 31:37.230
It's tragic.

722
31:37.600 --> 31:38.800
It's heartbreaking.

723
31:39.270 --> 31:40.720
It's infuriating.

724
31:44.230 --> 31:45.630
What a devastating loss.

725
31:45.750 --> 31:47.580
Doesn't that break your heart?

726
31:48.120 --> 31:50.780
Isn't that enough to show something went wrong?

727
31:53.600 --> 31:55.060
After the two armies joined forces,

728
31:55.060 --> 31:57.200
I spoke with cadres and soldiers of the Central Red Army

729
31:57.200 --> 31:58.710
to find out what had happened.

730
31:58.710 --> 31:59.920
Along the way,

731
32:00.280 --> 32:03.760
they faced a very complex situation.

732
32:04.070 --> 32:05.470
There were many things

733
32:05.550 --> 32:07.190
that we still didn't fully understand.

734
32:07.190 --> 32:09.790
It's too one-sided to look only at the numbers.

735
32:14.070 --> 32:14.880
Fine.

736
32:15.070 --> 32:17.600
Then I'll tell you something that's not one-sided.

737
32:17.600 --> 32:19.310
After the armies joined forces,

738
32:19.310 --> 32:22.680
when I heard Zhu De was suffering from back pain,

739
32:23.710 --> 32:27.880
I brought him the best

740
32:28.230 --> 32:29.490
medicated patch I could find,

741
32:29.490 --> 32:31.200
in the middle of the night.

742
32:31.620 --> 32:33.900
I put it on for him myself.

743
32:34.510 --> 32:36.310
And how did he treat me in return?

744
32:36.990 --> 32:38.710
Right in front of everyone,

745
32:40.270 --> 32:41.750
he slammed his hand down on the table.

746
32:41.750 --> 32:42.360
He...

747
32:42.780 --> 32:45.400
He humiliated me in front of everyone!

748
32:46.400 --> 32:48.350
Fine. I could put up with that.

749
32:48.960 --> 32:51.800
How much effort did our 4th Front Army

750
32:52.270 --> 32:53.760
put into welcoming them?

751
32:54.870 --> 32:56.760
You all know that, don't you?

752
32:57.360 --> 32:58.090
We made salt,

753
32:58.230 --> 32:59.160
spun yarn,

754
32:59.400 --> 33:01.880
and even knitted sweaters for them.

755
33:02.120 --> 33:02.870
Why?

756
33:05.200 --> 33:07.400
Because we were worried they'd be cold.

757
33:08.200 --> 33:09.260
And what happened?

758
33:09.750 --> 33:11.790
They left without a word.

759
33:11.920 --> 33:12.790
Fine.

760
33:13.440 --> 33:15.360
I could put up with that, too.

761
33:15.840 --> 33:17.710
I've put up with it time and again.

762
33:18.400 --> 33:21.440
But when they turn a deaf ear to what I say,

763
33:21.710 --> 33:23.470
when they just brush me aside,

764
33:23.880 --> 33:25.210
I can't take it anymore!

765
33:26.070 --> 33:27.390
I just can't take it!

766
33:33.120 --> 33:34.160
Back then,

767
33:34.510 --> 33:35.310
I...

768
33:37.960 --> 33:38.680
We...

769
33:39.840 --> 33:41.300
When we founded the Party,

770
33:41.490 --> 33:43.090
times were incredibly hard.

771
33:43.680 --> 33:45.600
Perhaps you don't know just how hard.

772
33:45.600 --> 33:47.070
But the three of us,

773
33:47.090 --> 33:51.020
when the national revolutionary movement was at its lowest point,

774
33:51.270 --> 33:53.180
built the 4th Front Army

775
33:53.510 --> 33:55.710
into a strong force.

776
33:56.030 --> 33:57.760
You know well how much hardship

777
33:57.790 --> 33:59.440
we went through, don't you?

778
33:59.560 --> 34:02.790
I'm doing this regardless of what it may do to my reputation!

779
34:02.790 --> 34:06.090
I can't let our cause come to nothing!

780
34:18.280 --> 34:20.429
Who understands what I'm going through?

781
34:20.429 --> 34:23.380
Few people share my convictions.

782
35:23.320 --> 35:24.150
Of course.

783
35:24.680 --> 35:27.720
People are bound to have different views.

784
35:28.320 --> 35:30.240
It takes time for everyone

785
35:30.730 --> 35:31.880
to figure this out.

786
35:32.510 --> 35:33.570
It doesn't matter.

787
35:34.840 --> 35:35.760
I can wait.

788
35:36.720 --> 35:38.520
Today's resolution and the list

789
35:38.790 --> 35:39.630
can...

790
35:42.270 --> 35:44.130
can remain confidential for now.

791
35:44.590 --> 35:46.240
Once we've moved south successfully

792
35:46.240 --> 35:47.760
and the situation has stabilized,

793
35:47.760 --> 35:50.240
we'll find a way to contact the Communist International.

794
35:50.240 --> 35:53.700
It won't be too late to announce it once we have their approval.

795
35:59.190 --> 36:02.470
Look, I've spoiled the meal

796
36:02.660 --> 36:04.570
with my temper.

797
36:05.360 --> 36:06.760
You two go back first,

798
36:06.970 --> 36:09.100
and think carefully about what I said.

799
36:16.970 --> 36:18.620
Xiangqian, Changhao.

800
36:20.470 --> 36:21.960
I, Zhang Guotao,

801
36:23.760 --> 36:26.190
have never asked anyone for anything in my life.

802
36:26.190 --> 36:29.250
I hope you'll understand my well-meaning intentions.

803
36:29.400 --> 36:31.400
As I said at the meeting,

804
36:32.150 --> 36:33.240
I believe

805
36:33.770 --> 36:35.570
a successful southward advance

806
36:36.400 --> 36:37.760
will prove me right.

807
37:52.990 --> 37:54.190
Have you eaten?

808
37:57.760 --> 37:59.670
Chairman Zhang, I've eaten.

809
38:05.400 --> 38:06.660
Come over and sit down.

810
38:11.070 --> 38:12.110
Yes.

811
38:18.630 --> 38:19.670
Eat.

812
38:28.630 --> 38:30.190
Dig in.

813
38:36.190 --> 38:37.050
Keep eating.

814
38:39.070 --> 38:41.720
Chairman Zhang, I really have eaten.

815
39:08.800 --> 39:09.630
Who is it?

816
39:10.320 --> 39:12.030
It's me, Liu Bocheng.

817
39:17.040 --> 39:17.920
Comrade Bocheng.

818
39:17.080 --> 39:19.980
[Liu Shaocwen, Political Instructor of the Red Army Headquarters]

819
39:23.760 --> 39:25.070
You're still up at this hour?

820
39:25.070 --> 39:26.070
Comrade Shaowen,

821
39:26.440 --> 39:27.970
I need to ask you something.

822
39:28.590 --> 39:30.510
I hope you'll be honest with me.

823
39:31.320 --> 39:32.070
Go ahead.

824
39:32.400 --> 39:34.600
What do you think of Zhang Guotao's move

825
39:34.870 --> 39:35.820
to establish a new Central Committee?

826
39:35.820 --> 39:37.550
I firmly opposed it, of course.

827
39:40.240 --> 39:41.670
But he did offer to make you

828
39:41.670 --> 39:44.920
Secretary-General of his so-called Central Committee.

829
39:46.240 --> 39:47.240
Comrade Bocheng,

830
39:47.760 --> 39:48.840
you know me well.

831
39:49.440 --> 39:50.670
From the very beginning,

832
39:50.670 --> 39:53.400
I've disliked Zhang Guotao's way of doing things.

833
39:53.400 --> 39:53.840
Here.

834
39:55.280 --> 39:57.760
If you and Commander-in-Chief Zhu hadn't told me

835
39:57.760 --> 39:58.640
to be patient,

836
39:58.660 --> 40:00.120
I would have quit long ago.

837
40:00.330 --> 40:02.990
And now he wants to make me "Secretary-General of the Central Committee?"

838
40:02.990 --> 40:04.650
I have no interest in it at all.

839
40:08.100 --> 40:09.880
You didn't come to me in the middle of the night

840
40:09.880 --> 40:11.740
just to ask me about that, did you?

841
40:16.240 --> 40:19.470
There's something very important I need to discuss with you.

842
40:19.470 --> 40:20.470
Go ahead.

843
40:21.070 --> 40:22.030
Do you still have

844
40:22.320 --> 40:24.400
the codebook we used to contact

845
40:24.800 --> 40:26.280
the Communist International?

846
40:26.280 --> 40:26.990
Yes.

847
40:27.280 --> 40:28.050
Wait a moment.

848
40:28.050 --> 40:28.640
Okay.

849
40:35.400 --> 40:36.400
Here it is.

850
40:38.920 --> 40:40.580
I've kept it with me all along.

851
40:46.110 --> 40:48.190
Does anyone else know about this?

852
40:48.400 --> 40:49.330
Absolutely not.

853
40:50.360 --> 40:51.130
Burn it.

854
40:53.360 --> 40:54.090
Understood.

855
40:57.430 --> 40:59.500
As the Central Committee led the Shaanxi-Gansu Detachment

856
40:59.500 --> 41:01.390
toward Shaanxi and Gansu,

857
41:01.960 --> 41:04.840
Zhang Guotao issued the "Suijing-Danba-Chonghua-Maogong Campaign Plan"

858
41:04.840 --> 41:07.900
on October 7, 1935.

859
41:08.360 --> 41:09.720
According to this plan,

860
41:09.780 --> 41:12.750
the southward-bound Red Army split into left and right columns,

861
41:12.750 --> 41:15.410
pushing forward simultaneously on both sides of the Dajinchuan River.

862
41:15.410 --> 41:17.070
Working in close coordination,

863
41:17.070 --> 41:19.590
they were to capture Suijing, Chonghua,

864
41:19.960 --> 41:21.790
Danba and Maogong one after another.

865
41:21.790 --> 41:24.380
Danba, Fubian, Maogong and other places

866
41:24.470 --> 41:26.800
would then serve as the bases for their southward push

867
41:26.800 --> 41:29.330
to capture the fertile lands around Chengdu.

868
41:29.590 --> 41:30.960
At this time,

869
41:29.650 --> 41:35.180
[Chengdu, Sichuan]

870
41:31.880 --> 41:35.080
we are facing both internal crises and external threats.

871
41:35.920 --> 41:39.470
We have reached the defining moment to enforce the principle of

872
41:39.840 --> 41:42.070
"internal pacification before external resistance."

873
41:42.070 --> 41:44.880
And there are 80,000 Communist soldiers heading south.

874
41:44.880 --> 41:46.840
Whether they cross the Min River

875
41:46.960 --> 41:48.030
to strike east,

876
41:48.420 --> 41:51.350
or take Maogong and Danba

877
41:51.440 --> 41:52.630
to strike south,

878
41:53.070 --> 41:55.730
they will inevitably push into western Sichuan

879
41:55.880 --> 41:57.440
and threaten Chengdu.

880
41:58.190 --> 41:59.630
Gentlemen, you know

881
41:59.800 --> 42:01.930
that Xu Xiangqian's Communist troops

882
42:02.400 --> 42:04.730
are wreaking havoc in the Daba Mountains.

883
42:05.320 --> 42:07.670
You besieged his forces from six directions,

884
42:07.670 --> 42:09.500
yet still let him slip away.

885
42:10.470 --> 42:12.320
What if the Communist troops come this time

886
42:12.320 --> 42:13.380
and decide to stay?

887
42:13.670 --> 42:15.470
What if they put down roots here?

888
42:15.990 --> 42:18.360
They would seize your territory

889
42:18.360 --> 42:19.590
and live off your grain.

890
42:19.590 --> 42:21.320
Would you allow that to happen?

891
42:25.990 --> 42:26.990
Gentlemen.

892
42:27.590 --> 42:30.880
Sichuan is the heartland of the country.

893
42:31.920 --> 42:34.380
This strategic area along the Yangtze River

894
42:35.590 --> 42:37.880
must be defended by fortifying our positions and clearing the fields.

895
42:37.880 --> 42:39.150
Only then will the Nationalist Government

896
42:39.150 --> 42:42.650
and I, as Generalissimo, have confidence in Sichuan’s defenses.

897
42:42.650 --> 42:45.850
Therefore, today, I hereby announce

898
42:46.400 --> 42:48.400
the Central Military Commission's

899
42:48.630 --> 42:50.030
decision.

900
42:50.510 --> 42:54.960
The Generalissimo's field headquarters will be moved from Wuchang to Chongqing.

901
42:54.960 --> 42:57.680
We will also dispatch military and political officials

902
42:57.680 --> 42:59.910
to help reorganize the Sichuan Army,

903
43:00.470 --> 43:02.150
and raise its combat

904
43:02.470 --> 43:04.440
effectiveness across the board.
